Stream API enables functional-style operations on collections (lazy, pipelined).

Key operations:
- Intermediate (lazy): filter(), map(), flatMap(), sorted(), distinct(), limit(), peek()
- Terminal (eager): collect(), forEach(), reduce(), count(), findFirst(), anyMatch(), toList()

Examples:
// Filter and collect
List<String> seniors = employees.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getAge() > 30)
    .map(Employee::getName)
    .sorted()
    .collect(Collectors.toList());

// Reduce
int total = numbers.stream().reduce(0, Integer::sum);

// Group by
Map<String, List<Employee>> byDept = employees.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Employee::getDept));

Parallel streams: stream().parallel() — use with caution; overhead for small collections.
